<div id="wrap" class="oe_structure">
<section class="s_text_block o_colored_level pt80 pb64" data-snippet="s_text_block" data-name="The name" style="background-color:#ede6d8;color:#1e1d1b">
<div class="container s_allow_columns">
<div style="max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;text-align:center">
<p style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5e5a52;margin:0 0 20px">The name</p>
<h1 style="font-family:Marcellus,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(34px,4.4vw,60px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 24px">Deep in Thoth</h1>
<p style="font-size:18px;line-height:30px;margin:0">Read it aloud and it sounds like deep in thought. Underneath is Thoth, called Djehuty in Egypt, the god of writing, wisdom and the moon, whom scribes claimed as their patron. The person wearing this is a thinker, and the clothes are a place to think.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="s_text_block o_colored_level pt32 pb64" data-snippet="s_text_block" data-name="The calendar" style="background-color:#ede6d8;color:#1e1d1b">
<div class="container s_allow_columns">
<div class="row align-items-center">
<div class="col-lg-6 pb32"><img src="%%att:dit-plate-moon.svg%%" alt="Stencil of the moon, its shadow slowly moving across the face" style="display:block;width:100%;aspect-ratio:4/3;object-fit:cover;background-color:#161b2a"/></div>
<div class="col-lg-6 pb32">
<p style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5e5a52;margin:0 0 12px">I · The calendar</p>
<h2 style="font-family:Marcellus,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:28px;line-height:34px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 16px">Thoth names the new year</h2>
<p style="font-size:16px;line-height:26px;margin:0 0 12px">The first month of the old Egyptian calendar, Thout, is named for him. It begins around September 11, at the start of the flood season.</p>
<p style="font-size:16px;line-height:26px;margin:0">So the brand keeps the same year. Every September a flagship Thout drop opens it, each one paired with a different desert of the world.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="s_text_block o_colored_level pt32 pb64" data-snippet="s_text_block" data-name="The journey" style="background-color:#ede6d8;color:#1e1d1b">
<div class="container s_allow_columns">
<div class="row align-items-center">
<div class="col-lg-6 pb32 order-lg-2"><img src="%%att:dit-flight.svg%%" alt="A sacred ibis flies in over the reeds at night, wings spread" style="display:block;width:100%;aspect-ratio:4/3;object-fit:cover;background-color:#11141c"/></div>
<div class="col-lg-6 pb32 order-lg-1">
<p style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5e5a52;margin:0 0 12px">II · The journey</p>
<h2 style="font-family:Marcellus,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:28px;line-height:34px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 16px">Thoth goes into the desert</h2>
<p style="font-size:16px;line-height:26px;margin:0 0 12px">In one myth, Ra sends Thoth to bring the Distant Goddess home from a remote desert. He does it with humility and cunning rather than force.</p>
<p style="font-size:16px;line-height:26px;margin:0">That is the founding image here: go deep into the desert, and come back with something worth carrying.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="s_text_block o_colored_level pt0 pb0" data-snippet="s_text_block" data-name="Reed strip" style="background-color:#ede6d8">
<img src="%%att:dit-reeds-strip.svg%%" alt="Papyrus and reeds along the water" style="display:block;width:100%;height:200px;object-fit:cover;object-position:50% 100%"/>
</section>
<section class="s_text_block o_colored_level pt64 pb64" data-snippet="s_text_block" data-name="Four things" style="background-color:#f6f1e7;color:#1e1d1b;border-top:1px solid #d6cbb6;border-bottom:1px solid #d6cbb6">
<div class="container s_allow_columns">
<h2 style="font-family:Marcellus,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:28px;line-height:34px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 32px">Four things in every piece</h2>
<div class="row">
<div class="col-lg-3 col-md-6 pb32"><div style="border-top:1px solid #1e1d1b;padding-top:16px"><h3 style="font-family:Marcellus,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:20px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 10px">Desert</h3><p style="font-size:16px;line-height:26px;margin:0">Sand, stone and sun-faded colour. Wide shapes that move air.</p></div></div>
<div class="col-lg-3 col-md-6 pb32"><div style="border-top:1px solid #1e1d1b;padding-top:16px"><h3 style="font-family:Marcellus,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:20px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 10px">City</h3><p style="font-size:16px;line-height:26px;margin:0">Streetwear cuts, mineral wash, type on the back. Each desert meets a city: Mojave and Los Angeles first.</p></div></div>
<div class="col-lg-3 col-md-6 pb32"><div style="border-top:1px solid #1e1d1b;padding-top:16px"><h3 style="font-family:Marcellus,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:20px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 10px">Word</h3><p style="font-size:16px;line-height:26px;margin:0">One written idea per piece: a framework, a question, a line worth keeping.</p></div></div>
<div class="col-lg-3 col-md-6 pb32"><div style="border-top:1px solid #1e1d1b;padding-top:16px"><h3 style="font-family:Marcellus,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:20px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 10px">Comfort</h3><p style="font-size:16px;line-height:26px;margin:0">Natural fibres first, cut oversized and relaxed, made to be worn often and kept long.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="made" class="s_text_block o_colored_level pt80 pb80" data-snippet="s_text_block" data-name="How it is made" style="background-color:#ede6d8;color:#1e1d1b">
<div class="container s_allow_columns">
<div class="row">
<div class="col-lg-5 pb32">
<p style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5e5a52;margin:0 0 12px">How it is made</p>
<h2 style="font-family:Marcellus,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:28px;line-height:34px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 16px">Never fast fashion</h2>
<p style="font-size:16px;line-height:26px;margin:0">A promise you can check. Here is what it means in practice.</p>
</div>
<div class="col-lg-7 pb32">
<div style="border-top:1px solid #1e1d1b;padding:20px 0" class="row"><div class="col-md-5" style="font-weight:600">Make only what is sold</div><div class="col-md-7">Pre-order windows. Printed after payment. No restocking a graphic to chase volume.</div></div>
<div style="border-top:1px solid #d6cbb6;padding:20px 0" class="row"><div class="col-md-5" style="font-weight:600">Natural fibres first</div><div class="col-md-7">100% cotton now; linen and plant-dyed indigo as the brand grows. Any blend is named on the product page.</div></div>
<div style="border-top:1px solid #d6cbb6;padding:20px 0" class="row"><div class="col-md-5" style="font-weight:600">Know the supply chain</div><div class="col-md-7">Each page says what the blank is and where it was washed and printed.</div></div>
<div style="border-top:1px solid #d6cbb6;border-bottom:1px solid #d6cbb6;padding:20px 0" class="row"><div class="col-md-5" style="font-weight:600">Made to keep</div><div class="col-md-7">A care card in every order: wash cold, hang dry.</div></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="s_text_block o_colored_level pt64 pb64" data-snippet="s_text_block" data-name="Next" style="background-color:#263357;color:#ede6d8">
<div class="container s_allow_columns">
<div class="d-flex flex-wrap justify-content-between align-items-center" style="gap:24px">
<h2 style="font-family:Marcellus,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:28px;line-height:34px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#ede6d8;margin:0">Drop 01 is coming</h2>
